==Trivia==
*Nekondo SP bears a striking resemblance to SNK's [[wikia:snk:Kim Kaphwan|Kim Kaphwan]].
*In the Nintendo Switch version, it only has its normal and evolved forms while under a different name, that being Taekwondo Cat and HG Taekwondo Cat respectively.
*It, [[Baozi Cat (Special Cat)|Baozi Cat]], [[Crazed Baozi Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Baozi Cat]], [[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Li'l Valkyrie]], and [[Li'l Valkyrie Dark (Uber Rare Cat)|Li'l Valkyrie Dark]], are part of a version exclusive in The Battle Cats Unite, as they can only be obtained normally via purchasing the Southeast Asia version.
*Nekondo in The Battle Cats Unite! has a maximum level up 30+20, however the +20 level cap is impossible to view naturally and is obtainable via save file editing.

